title: घञ् vs. अच्  प्रत्ययः

!!The Difference in Meaning (The Sense of the Affix)
The core difference lies in the Sūtras (rules) that apply and the sense (artha) that the affix conveys:

;A. घञ् (Ghañ) Affix


<<<
The घञ् affix is primarily governed by the rule भावे (P. 3.3.18), meaning it often forms a noun denoting the action or state itself (the abstract idea).

Sense: भावः (Bhāvaḥ) — The action, state, or abstract idea of the root.

Meaning: Seeing (the act of seeing), vision, or the sight itself (abstractly).

Examples: Darśanaṁ (seeing), Sparśaḥ (touching).

<<<

;B. अच् (Ac) Affix


<<<
The अच् affix is governed by various rules (e.g., P. 3.1.134) and typically forms a noun denoting the agent, the instrument, or the object of the action, or a habitual action.

Sense: कर्तृ, करण, अधिकरणम् (Kartṛ, Karaṇa, Adhikaraṇam) — The agent (doer), instrument (means), or locus (place) of the action.

Meaning: One who sees (agent), that by which one sees (instrument/eye), or the place of seeing (locus).
 <<<


|Feature	|घञ् (दर्शः)	|अच् (दर्शः)|h
|Pāṇini's Rule	|Primarily भावे (P. 3.3.18)	|Varies (e.g., P. 3.1.134)|
|Conveyed Sense	|Action/State (The Act of Seeing)	|Agent/Instrument/Locus (One who sees, the means of sight)|
|Practical Use	|दर्शनस्य (of the seeing)	|द्रष्टा (the seer)|
<<<
<<<

In classical use, both forms may overlap in meaning, but घञ् emphasizes the action (abstract noun), while अच् emphasizes the performer or tool related to the action.